  "content": {
    "id": "p18-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "",
    "prompt": "Use trigonometric identities and factoring to solve for $0^\\circ\\le\\alpha\\le360^\\circ$, giving solutions correct to the nearest minute where necessary.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sec^2\\alpha=2\\sec\\alpha$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\alpha=60^\\circ,300^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\cos^2\\alpha}&=\\frac{2}{\\cos\\alpha}\\\\1&=2\\cos\\alpha\\\\\\cos\\alpha&=\\frac12\\\\\\alpha&=60^\\circ,300^\\circ.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\sec^2\\alpha-\\tan\\alpha-3=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\alpha=63^\\circ26',135^\\circ,243^\\circ26',315^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\tan^2\\alpha+1-\\tan\\alpha-3&=0\\\\\\tan^2\\alpha-\\tan\\alpha-2&=0\\\\(\\tan\\alpha-2)(\\tan\\alpha+1)&=0.\\end{aligned}$$\nThus $\\tan\\alpha=2$ or $\\tan\\alpha=-1$.\n$$\\alpha=63^\\circ26',135^\\circ,243^\\circ26',315^\\circ.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\operatorname{cosec}^3 2\\alpha=4\\operatorname{cosec}2\\alpha$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\alpha=15^\\circ,75^\\circ,105^\\circ,165^\\circ,195^\\circ,255^\\circ,285^\\circ,345^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosec}^3 2\\alpha&=4\\operatorname{cosec}2\\alpha\\\\\\operatorname{cosec}2\\alpha(\\operatorname{cosec}^2 2\\alpha-4)&=0\\\\\\operatorname{cosec}2\\alpha&=\\pm2\\\\\\sin2\\alpha&=\\pm\\frac12.\\end{aligned}$$\nHere $\\operatorname{cosec}2\\alpha\\ne0$ and $0^\\circ\\le2\\alpha\\le720^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}2\\alpha&=30^\\circ,150^\\circ,210^\\circ,330^\\circ,\\\\&\\quad390^\\circ,510^\\circ,570^\\circ,690^\\circ\\\\\\alpha&=15^\\circ,75^\\circ,105^\\circ,165^\\circ,\\\\&\\quad195^\\circ,255^\\circ,285^\\circ,345^\\circ.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\sqrt3\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\left(\\dfrac\\alpha2\\right)+\\cot\\left(\\dfrac\\alpha2\\right)=\\sqrt3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\alpha=180^\\circ,240^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt3\\left(1+\\cot^2\\frac\\alpha2\\right)+\\cot\\frac\\alpha2&=\\sqrt3\\\\\\sqrt3\\cot^2\\frac\\alpha2+\\cot\\frac\\alpha2&=0\\\\\\cot\\frac\\alpha2\\left(\\sqrt3\\cot\\frac\\alpha2+1\\right)&=0.\\end{aligned}$$\nThus $\\cot\\dfrac\\alpha2=0$ or $\\cot\\dfrac\\alpha2=-\\dfrac1{\\sqrt3}$.\nFor $0^\\circ\\le\\dfrac\\alpha2\\le180^\\circ$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\cot\\frac\\alpha2=0:&\\quad\\frac\\alpha2=90^\\circ,\\quad\\alpha=180^\\circ;\\\\\\cot\\frac\\alpha2=-\\frac1{\\sqrt3}:&\\quad\\frac\\alpha2=120^\\circ,\\quad\\alpha=240^\\circ.\\end{aligned}$$\nTherefore $\\alpha=180^\\circ$ or $240^\\circ$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 65
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\sqrt3\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\alpha=4\\cot\\alpha$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\alpha=30^\\circ,60^\\circ,210^\\circ,240^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt3}{\\sin^2\\alpha}&=\\frac{4\\cos\\alpha}{\\sin\\alpha}\\\\\\sqrt3&=4\\cos\\alpha\\sin\\alpha\\\\\\sqrt3&=2\\sin2\\alpha\\\\\\sin2\\alpha&=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\2\\alpha&=60^\\circ,120^\\circ,420^\\circ,480^\\circ\\\\\\alpha&=30^\\circ,60^\\circ,210^\\circ,240^\\circ.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 49
      },
      {
        "id": "p18-q12-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\cot\\alpha+3\\tan\\alpha=5\\operatorname{cosec}\\alpha$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\alpha=60^\\circ,300^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\cos\\alpha}{\\sin\\alpha}+\\frac{3\\sin\\alpha}{\\cos\\alpha}&=\\frac5{\\sin\\alpha}\\\\\\cos^2\\alpha+3\\sin^2\\alpha&=5\\cos\\alpha\\\\\\cos^2\\alpha+3(1-\\cos^2\\alpha)&=5\\cos\\alpha\\\\3-2\\cos^2\\alpha&=5\\cos\\alpha\\\\2\\cos^2\\alpha+5\\cos\\alpha-3&=0\\\\(2\\cos\\alpha-1)(\\cos\\alpha+3)&=0.\\end{aligned}$$\nThus $\\cos\\alpha=\\dfrac12$; reject $\\cos\\alpha=-3$ since $-1\\le\\cos\\alpha\\le1$.\n$$\\alpha=60^\\circ,300^\\circ.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 63
      }
    ]
  },
